> DMS Settings - Bar and Dock

In-depth guide to DMS bar and dock settings (super+S > dank bar, dock and launcher).

### Bar Position

choose which bars are active: top bar, bottom bar, status bar, side bar.
each bar has its own configuration for widgets and appearance.

SNAPS-OS comes with 4 pre-configured bars that can be toggled via *super+shift+D*.
you can combine multiple bars (e.g. top bar + bottom bar).

### Autohide

bars can be set to autohide. configure:
autohide delay: how long to wait before hiding.
autohide sensitivity: how close to the edge to trigger show.
autohide height: pixels of edge area that triggers show.

### Bar Widgets

each bar can show these widgets:

launcher: app launcher button (top-left menu).
clock: date and time display (configurable format).
system tray: notification area for background apps.
workspace: workspace/tag indicator and switcher.
media: now-playing media player widget.
notifications: notification indicator and history.
system stats: CPU, RAM, network usage.
quick settings: brightness, volume, network toggles.
weather: current weather display.
dash button: quick access to the dash panel.

### Dock Behavior

dock position: bottom, left, or right edge.
dock autohide: similar to bar autohide settings.
dock icon size: small, medium, large.
dock pinned apps: apps that always appear in the dock.
dock running indicators: show which apps are running.
dock smart hiding: hide when a window overlaps it.

### Icon Settings

icon theme: currently set to tela-circle-icon-theme-black.
icon size preferences for both bar and dock.
